          "diff_hunk": "mmutableMap.of(\"bucket\", \"b1\"), \"op-1\", differentMetric);\n+    ImmutableSet<Object> operations = ImmutableSet.of(base);\n+\n+    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentName);\n+    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentAttributes);\n+    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentOperationId);\n+    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentDurationMetric);\n+    assertThat(operations).doesNotContain(\"READ\");",
          "body": "![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)\n\nUsing `ImmutableSet.doesNotContain` to assert inequality against a different type is indirect and requires creating an intermediate set. Directly asserting `assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(\"READ\")` is cleaner, more readable, and avoids the unnecessary collection allocation.\n\n```suggestion\n    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentName);\n    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentAttributes);\n    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentOperationId);\n    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(differentDurationMetric);\n    assertThat(base).isNotEqualTo(\"READ\");\n```",
